# Helpdesk — Project Memory

## What this project is
An internal helpdesk platform for support agents to manage tickets, powered by AI (Claude) for classification, summaries, and suggested replies. Tickets can arrive via email or be created manually.

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Choice |
|---|---|
| Runtime | Bun |
| Frontend | React 19 + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind CSS v3 + React Router v7 |
| UI Components | shadcn/ui (Default style, Neutral theme, CSS variables) |
| Forms | react-hook-form v7 + zod v4 + @hookform/resolvers |
| Backend | Express 5 + TypeScript (runs on Bun) |
| Database | PostgreSQL via Prisma ORM |
| Auth | Better Auth (`better-auth`) |
| AI | Anthropic Claude API |
| Email | SendGrid or Mailgun |
| E2E Testing | Playwright (`@playwright/test`) |
| Component testing | Vitest + React Testing Library + `@testing-library/jest-dom` (jsdom via Vite) |
| Rate Limiting | `express-rate-limit` (production only) |
| Client HTTP | **axios** (not `fetch`) |
| Client server state | **TanStack Query** (`@tanstack/react-query`) |
| Shared code | **`core`** workspace package (`packages/core`) — Zod schemas and types used by both client and server |

## Monorepo Structure

```
helpdesk/
├── e2e/                     # Playwright E2E tests
│   ├── global-setup.ts      # Runs prisma migrate deploy on helpdesk_test before suite
│   └── global-teardown.ts   # Resets test DB on CI after suite
├── playwright.config.ts     # Playwright config — loads server/.env.test, spins up both servers
├── packages/
│   └── core/                # Shared Zod schemas + inferred types; export via package name `core`
├── client/                  # React app (port 5173)
│   ├── components.json      # shadcn config
│   └── src/
│       ├── components/
│       │   ├── ui/          # shadcn components (button, card, form, input, label, alert)
│       │   ├── Layout.tsx   # App shell with sidebar nav and header
│       │   ├── ProtectedRoute.tsx  # Redirects unauthenticated users to /login
│       │   └── AdminRoute.tsx      # Redirects non-ADMIN users to /dashboard
│       ├── lib/
│       │   ├── utils.ts     # cn() helper (clsx + tailwind-merge)
│       │   └── auth-client.ts
│       ├── pages/
│       │   ├── LoginPage.tsx
│       │   ├── DashboardPage.tsx
│       │   ├── UsersPage.tsx       # Admin-only; route: /users
│       │   └── UsersPage.test.tsx  # Colocated component tests (`*.test.tsx`)
│       ├── test/
│       │   ├── setup.ts            # Vitest: jest-dom matchers (`@testing-library/jest-dom/vitest`)
│       │   └── render.tsx          # `renderWithProviders` (QueryClientProvider + test QueryClient)
│       └── App.tsx
└── server/                  # Express API (port 8080)
    ├── .env.test            # Test env (gitignored) — points to helpdesk_test DB
    ├── .env.test.example    # Committed template for .env.test
    ├── prisma/
    │   ├── schema.prisma
    │   └── seed.ts          # Creates admin user (SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL / SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD)
    └── src/
        ├── app.ts           # Express factory
        ├── index.ts         # Entry point
        ├── routes/
        ├── middleware/
        │   └── rateLimiter.ts  # authLimiter (20 req/15min) + apiLimiter (200 req/15min)
        └── lib/
            ├── prisma.ts
            └── auth.ts      # Better Auth config (emailAndPassword, disableSignUp: true)
```

- Vite proxies `/api/*` → `http://localhost:8080`
- Run everything: `bun dev:server` and `bun dev:client` from root
- **`bun install` from the repo root** links workspaces (`client`, `server`, `packages/core`). Client and server depend on **`core`** via `"core": "workspace:*"` — import shared schemas from `"core"` (e.g. `createUserBodySchema`, `CreateUserBody`)
- **`main.tsx`** wraps the app with `QueryClientProvider` (shared `QueryClient` with sensible `defaultOptions`, e.g. `staleTime` for queries)

## Prisma Models
`User` (id, email, name, password, role: ADMIN|AGENT)
`Ticket` (id, subject, body, status, category, priority, assignedTo, replies)
`Reply` (id, body, isAi, sentEmail, ticketId)

## Auth
- Better Auth is configured in `server/src/lib/auth.ts`
- `emailAndPassword` is enabled; public sign-up is disabled (`disableSignUp: true`) — users must be seeded
- `role` is declared as `user.additionalFields` in the server auth config so it is included in session payloads
- `auth-client.ts` uses `inferAdditionalFields` plugin (manual declaration) to expose `role` on the client session type
- Route protection: `ProtectedRoute` (auth check) wraps all app routes; `AdminRoute` (role check) wraps admin-only routes
- The sidebar nav conditionally renders admin links based on `session.user.role === "ADMIN"`

