| Email | Password | Role |
|---|---|---|
| (set via SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL env) | (set via SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD env) | ADMIN |
| agent@example.com | password@123 | AGENT |

## Rate Limiting
- Applied in `app.ts` only when `NODE_ENV === "production"`
- `authLimiter`: 20 requests / 15 min on `/api/auth` (login, session endpoints)
- `apiLimiter`: 200 requests / 15 min on all other `/api` routes
- Uses `RateLimit-*` response headers (`draft-8` standard)
- Inactive in development and test environments

## E2E Testing
- Use the **`playwright-e2e-writer` subagent** to write all Playwright tests — invoke it with: _"Use the playwright-e2e-writer to write tests for [feature]"_
- Tests live in `e2e/*.spec.ts`; run with `bun run test:e2e` from the repo root
- See the `playwright-e2e-writer` agent (`.cursor/agents/playwright-e2e-writer.md`) for full setup details, conventions, and code patterns

## Component testing (Vitest + React Testing Library)
- **Run (repo root):** `bun run test:client` — runs all client Vitest tests once (`vitest run` in `client/`)
- **Run (client package):** `bun run test` (CI-style single run) or `bun run test:watch` (watch mode)
- **Config:** `client/vite.config.ts` — `test.environment: "jsdom"`, `test.globals: true`, `test.setupFiles: "./src/test/setup.ts"`
- **Writing tests:** colocate `*.test.tsx` next to the component or page under test; use `@testing-library/react` (`screen`, `waitFor`, `within`, user-centric queries). Prefer roles and accessible names over CSS/test IDs unless necessary
- **Matchers:** `client/src/test/setup.ts` imports `@testing-library/jest-dom/vitest` so `expect(...).toBeInTheDocument()` and related matchers work
- **React Query:** wrap components that use `useQuery` / `useMutation` with `renderWithProviders` from `@/test/render` (test `QueryClient` uses `retry: false` and `gcTime: 0` so async tests stay deterministic)
- **HTTP:** mock `axios` (or the module under test) with `vi.mock` — preserve `importOriginal` when the component uses `axios.isAxiosError` or other helpers
- **Scope:** component tests cover UI states (loading, success, empty, error); cross-browser flows and real backends belong in Playwright E2E tests

## Conventions
- **Shared validation:** API request bodies and matching client forms should use the same Zod schema in **`packages/core`** (export from `core`) so rules and error messages stay in sync — avoid duplicating `z.object({...})` in `client/` and `server/`
- All server source files use ESM (`import/export`), `.js` extensions in imports
- Express route files export a typed `IRouter`; mount under `/api` in `app.ts`
- **Express 5 async errors:** Returned promises from route handlers are supported; if an `async` handler’s promise rejects, Express forwards the error to error-handling middleware (you do not need `try/catch` solely to avoid unhandled rejections). Use `try/catch` (or `catch` on a specific call) only when you must handle errors locally—e.g. map known errors to a specific status/body and `return` without calling `next(err)`.
- Prisma client is a singleton in `server/src/lib/prisma.ts`
- Frontend path alias `@/` maps to `client/src/`
- Tailwind brand color token: `brand-{50..900}` (blue scale) — preserved alongside shadcn tokens
- shadcn design tokens use CSS variables (`--background`, `--foreground`, `--primary`, etc.) defined in `src/index.css`
- Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for conditional className merging
- Forms use shadcn `<Form>` / `<FormField>` / `<FormControl>` / `<FormMessage>` wired to react-hook-form + zod
- Chrome autofill styles are suppressed globally via `:-webkit-autofill` overrides in `index.css`
- Role-based access: `ADMIN` manages users; `AGENT` handles tickets
- **Client data fetching:** use **axios** for API calls (`withCredentials: true` so Better Auth session cookies are sent to `/api/*`). Use **TanStack Query** (`useQuery`, `useMutation`, etc.) for server state, caching, and request/error lifecycle — do not use raw `useEffect` + `fetch` for routine API-backed UI unless there is a specific reason
